    "created_at": "2022-09-10T22:08:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-09-10T22:45:23Z",
    "body": "Looking at this again, I don't think we can report validation errors directly in the [ipv4-number-parser](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#ipv4-number-parser) as it is also used in Step 4 of [ends-in-a-number-checker](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#ends-in-a-number-checker). Doing so would cause the same validation error to be emitted twice in an edge case such as `https://0xF`. Reporting the validation error in [ipv4-number-parser](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#ipv4-number-parser) Step 6.3 would probably work better.\r\n\r\n> The IPv4 and IPv6 parsers should not be invoked directly. You always want to use the host parser. Perhaps we want to stress this some more somehow.\r\n\r\nAgreed. I was pretty sure that was the case, but I wasn't sure if the IPv4 parser was exported for other specs.\r\n\r\nFeel free to mark as \"good first issue\". If nobody wants to pick it up, I'd be happy to submit a patch.",
